<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Personal on Ugur's Personal Documentation</title><link>https://blog.ugurelveren.com/tags/personal/</link><description>Recent content in Personal on Ugur's Personal Documentation</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.ugurelveren.com/tags/personal/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Life Isn't Complicated. I Make It Complicated.</title><link>https://blog.ugurelveren.com/post/life-isnt-complicated-i-make-it-complicated/</link><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.ugurelveren.com/post/life-isnt-complicated-i-make-it-complicated/</guid><description>&lt;p>There are a few things I enjoy doing when I drive alone. What I choose depends on how far I&amp;rsquo;m going and how I&amp;rsquo;m feeling. If I&amp;rsquo;m heading somewhere far away (30 minutes or more, say), I love listening to audiobooks. On shorter drives, if I&amp;rsquo;m feeling good, I listen to music from my high school days. If it&amp;rsquo;s a short drive and I&amp;rsquo;m not feeling great, I either focus on the road or call someone to get my mind off things. But if I&amp;rsquo;m not feeling great and the drive is long, I fixate on what&amp;rsquo;s bothering me and jump from one thought to the next.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Travel</title><link>https://blog.ugurelveren.com/bucket-list/travel/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.ugurelveren.com/bucket-list/travel/</guid><description>&lt;table>
